<Page title="Donation integrity policy">
  <p>
    <strong>What this is.</strong> The Treaty Land Atlas is an educational and advocacy project by
    Benjamin Life (@omniharmonic). It points readers to ways of supporting Land Back: returning
    land, and authority over land, to Native nations. We do not receive, hold or process donations.
    We take no payment, commission, affiliate fee or data from any organization we list.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How we choose who to list.</strong> Before we list a group we check its legal identity
    and tax status in public registries, whether it has filed recent financial reports, the payee on
    its donation page, who leads it and whether they are Native people or a tribal government, and
    whether the nation whose land is concerned supports being named. If we cannot verify something,
    we say so, or we do not link to the group.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How we label.</strong> Each listing says whether it is a tribal government, a tribal or
    Native-led nonprofit, a fiscally sponsored project, or an allied organization that is not
    Native-led, and what we could and could not verify. “Self-described” means the group says it is
    Native-led and we have not independently confirmed it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What your money does.</strong> Large land returns are usually paid for by public
    programs, foundations and long negotiation. A gift supports an organization’s work; it does not
    buy a number of acres.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What we will never do.</strong> Use images or stories without consent, sell products or
    “adopt an acre” schemes, run donor leaderboards, promise outcomes, or send you to a person or
    group we have not checked.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Corrections and removal.</strong> If a listed organization, a tribal government or a
    community member asks us to change or remove a listing, we do so promptly.{' '}
    <a href={href('/corrections/')}>Contact us</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Limits.</strong> We are not tax or legal advisers. This policy is awaiting review by a
    lawyer.
  </p>
</Page>
